==Icelandic==
[[File:Iris - right eye of a girl.jpg|thumb|Eitt auga.]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈøyːɣa/|lang=is}} ({{audio|is-auga.ogg|listen}})
*: {{rhymes|øyːɣa|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|auga|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|augô|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|h₃ekʷ-||eye; to see|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognates include Latin {{term|oculus|lang=la}}, Sanskrit {{term|अक्षि|sc=Deva|tr=ákṣi|lang=sa}}, Gothic {{term|sc=Goth|𐌰𐌿𐌲𐍉|tr=áugō|lang=got}}, Old English {{term|eage|ēaġe|lang=ang}}, English {{term|eye|lang=en}}, Scots {{term|ee|lang=sco}}, Swedish {{term|öga|lang=sv}}, Danish {{term|øje|lang=da}}.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n|auga|augu}}

# [[eye]]
#* [[w:en:Hávamál|Hávamál]] ([[s:en:Poetic Edda/Hávamál|English source]], [[s:is:Hávamál|Icelandic sourve]])
#*: ''Inn vari gestur''
#*: ''er til verðar kemur''
#*: ''[[þegja þunnu hljóði|þunnu hljóði þegir]],''
#*: ''eyrum hlýðir,''
#*: ''en '''augum''' skoðar.''
#*: ''Svo nýsist fróðra hver fyrir.''
#*:: The knowing guest
#*:: who goes to the feast,
#*:: In silent attention sits;
#*:: With his ears he hears, 
#*:: with his '''eyes''' he watches,
#*:: Thus wary are wise men all. 

